      "testCases": [
        "disabled providers resolve without probing",
        "first reads return checking without blocking and start one background probe",
        "stale, available, unavailable, and checking remain distinct",
        "probe errors and timeouts become bounded unavailable health",
        "probe timeout aborts the exact provider check and leaves no active work",
        "every production provider forwards cancellation through launch resolution and executable probing",
        "repeated real executable probes are killed and reaped before abort settles",
        "concurrent fresh requests deduplicate per provider generation",
        "registry and config changes abort cached and in-flight generations",
        "repeated fresh and stale checks leave no provider work behind",
        "daemon status returns promptly while a provider probe hangs",
        "create, resume, import, draft, and reload fresh-probe only their requested provider",
        "reload rejects disabled and unavailable providers before session replacement",
        "draft commands and features reject before default-mode normalization",
        "checking remains optimistic for legacy clients while explicit status serves new clients",
        "stale last-known availability is excluded from current lifecycle alternatives",
        "unrelated provider failure cannot block requested-provider lifecycle",
        "provider snapshot timeout, refresh, config reset, destroy, and shutdown never overlap owned work",
        "provider health replacement waits for delayed abort cleanup and shutdown drains active probes",
        "timed-out executable wrappers and descendants are killed and reaped before replacement",
        "invalid executable timeout and buffer limits reject before spawning",
        "provider config success waits for live application and restores exact persisted state on failure",
        "unrelated daemon config changes do not restart or cancel provider catalog work"
